From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000006 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: rk-forge <rk-forge@localhost>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 23:40:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] input: goodix: sequence power before reset

The TOPEET vendor gt9xx driver enables the touch regulator, waits 20 ms,
and only then requests the GPIOs and performs the GT911 reset/address-select
sequence.  Preserve that power-on stabilization interval in the mainline
Goodix driver.

This matters on the RK3588 TOPEET 10.1-inch LCD/touch module, where an early
probe can start an I2C transfer before the shared module rail has stabilized.
The transfer then times out in the RK3x controller's START state, while a
later manual bind resets and identifies the same controller successfully.

Signed-off-by: rk-forge <rk-forge@localhost>
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c | 8 ++++++++
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
index 000000000000..000000000000 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/goodix.c
@@ -1362,6 +1362,14 @@ static int goodix_ts_probe(struct i2c_client *client)
 	if (error)
 		return error;
 
+	/*
+	 * The TOPEET GT911 vendor driver waits for the touch supply to settle
+	 * before starting the reset/address-selection sequence.  Without this
+	 * interval the RK3588 board can issue the first
+	 * I2C START while the integrated LCD/touch module is still powering up.
+	 */
+	msleep(20);
+
 reset:
 	if (ts->reset_controller_at_probe) {
 		/* reset the controller */
